{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01JTXgMFYFjYNfnGvok4d9z3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a single-user productivity system John runs locally. Grounded claims from the project docs:\n\n- **Purpose.** A personal task/productivity manager for J.C. Liechty â€” it tracks tasks, projects, an inbox, and per-domain work (academic, commercial, family, writing) across plain-text markdown files that are the single source of truth (no database, no syncing). Everything lives in one folder, `C:\\dev\\Anchor`.\n\n- **What it ships (core app).** `anchor_gui.py` â€” a self-contained Python stdlib HTTP server that generates a full browser dashboard at `http://localhost:8777`, reading/writing the markdown files directly. It runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor`. A CLI mirror (`anchor.py`) provides the same operations as one-shot commands and regenerates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Task lifecycle.** Tasks move through Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled / Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored, with optional Notes, priorities, energy levels, due dates, and domain tags â€” all editable from the browser or CLI.\n\n- **Self-testing.** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs daily at 5 AM (Task Scheduler), parsing every markdown file, booting a throwaway test server, exercising every endpoint and task state, and writing a dated report to `health_reports/`. It also walks the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces fully stubbed (never the live service or real `claude`).\n\n- **The R&D \"control surface\" (its largest subsystem, v2â†’v4).** A mission-control layer for \"trio-driven\" project work â€” the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman skill pipeline. Each project gets a window where lanes (Research Â· Planning Â· Build Â· Deliverables Â· Grass) show their most-recent session as a status-lit tile; clicking expands an inline panel with a cached, grounded summary plus a real **ConPTY terminal** (xterm.js over a hand-rolled WebSocket). Sessions are durable, git-worktree-isolated, engine-toggleable (Claudeâ†”Gemini), and survive restart. It also does per-lane doc-role mapping, cost/tokens/time rollups, grass-idea promotion, and type-aware deliverable launches.\n\n- **Notable constraint it honors.** Python-stdlib-only with exactly one declared exception â€” the optional `pywinpty` native dep, imported lazily in `pty_manager.py` only for the terminal subsystem, which degrades gracefully when absent. `distro.py` enforces this by refusing any other native/third-party import.\n\n- **Status.** v4 \"Project Cockpit\" was built (9 waves green, 637 tests) and merged to master on 2026-06-13; the current branch `foreman/rnd-v4.1-cockpit` is a follow-on iteration.\n\nOne caveat: this summary leans on `CLAUDE.md` and the locked North-Star anchors rather than re-reading the source â€” if you want any specific claim verified against the actual code, I can check it."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45330,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb45f770-8cae-4ee0-ad01-84348795cf62","uuid":"4d2cfdb8-e6f5-467b-8b55-8c3233a5b479","request_id":"req_011Cc1nUXDtc2xw6PoU8SXmd"}
